WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.290
Things You Missed In The Cloverfield Paradox
and ARG

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.710
A few days ago we were all sitting there watching
the Super Bowl and Bad Robot dropped a new

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:13.260
Cloverfield movie faster than Tom Brady managed
to drop that Lombardi Trophy.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.420
But before I can get into the Things You Missed
in this new Cloverfield movie, let's do a

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:23.160
quick quick recap of everything in the Cloverfield
films and ARG so far, because I will be referencing

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.270
back to them.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.869
If you aren't familiar with ARGs, it stands
for Alternate Reality Game.

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:32.800
In other words, it's a viral marketing technique
that was used to create buzz for each of these

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.290
movies, primarily through the creation of
websites and twitter accounts that live within

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.079
the Cloverfield universes.

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:41.940
They typically drop cryptic clues and leave
the fans to decipher their meaning to unlock

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.590
the next piece of the puzzle.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:48.380
And one other thing -- the Clover ARGs are
considered canon.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:53.480
So most of the ARG for the first Cloverfield
movie takes place on the Tagruato website.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.800
If you aren't familiar, Tagruato is a Japanese
mining company considered to be the most advanced

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.660
in the world and known for their deep sea
oil drilling stations that can drill miles

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.809
and miles further underwater than their competitors.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:09.140
Some people believe it is one of these drilling
stations in the Atlantic that awakened the

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.840
dormant Cloverfield monster, or possibly monsterS
in 2008.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.409
But aside from deep sea drilling, they also
own several subsidiary companies, like Yoshida

00:01:18.409 --> 00:01:22.210
Medical Research, a deep sea bioprospecting
company.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.580
What the heck does that mean?

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.570
Basically they study deep sea creatures in
extreme environments to see how they survive

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.860
and how that can be applied for human survival.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.250
Tagruato also owns a technology firm called
Bold Futura, which develops technology for

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.479
military and space exploration.

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:41.470
That includes developing satellites, so obviously
we'll be coming back to that one.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:42.990
Then there's ParafFun!

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:47.659
Wax Distributors, though it's unclear how
that one ties in with the other subsidiaries.

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:50.159
The last one is a beverage company called
Slusho!

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:54.970
the company that Rob, from the first Cloverfield,
was planning to move to Japan to manage.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:55.970
Slusho!

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:59.490
famously uses a secret ingredient called Deep
Sea Nectar known to make the consumer feel

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.190
happy and have numerous health benefits.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.369
Some people believe that this nectar is extracted
from the egg of the Cloverfield monster and

00:02:06.369 --> 00:02:10.160
that the drilling station in the Atlantic
near New York City is actually collecting

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.239
this nectar.

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:14.440
This is because the parasites that come off
of the monster are found to have high levels

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.230
of the nectar in their blood.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:20.950
That leads us into the first ARG which is
about a group of extreme environmental activists

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:26.230
known as TIDO Wave who go to this Atlantic
station to try to expose Tagruato for some

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:29.260
kind of dark secret that they are supposedly
hiding there.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:35.030
The station is destroyed in late 2007 and
Tagruato blames this extremist group for attacking

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.030
it.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.849
However I'll show you the video and let you
be the judge of what happened.

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:43.470
"The incident is being coined an environmental
disaster and a matter of life and death for

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:47.760
almost 300 individuals aboard the large deep
sea drilling platform.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.500
It went down days ago and only now are we
beginning to learn details regarding the oil

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.930
rig collapse and what may have caused such
a devastating accident.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:07.080
This dramatic home video captured by eyewitnesses
on the scene shows a large oil rig in the

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.080
middle of the Atlantic Ocean suddenly sinking
under violent and explained circumstances.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.040
The destruction of the Chiuai drilling station
happening dangerously close to the coast of

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.840
Connecticut sending hundreds of workers scrambling
for help as a large oil rig collapsed.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.920
Video footage shot earlier show signs oil
is possibly seeping from the big rig into

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:22.920
the sea.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:28.480
The dark shape below the surface appears to
be an oil spill that could easily mean a nightmare

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.570
for the shoreline of Connecticut.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.570
Yeah.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:32.930
Oil spill.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.930
Shortly after, this happens.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.830
The final extraordinary clip clearly shows
the sheer speed and power of the sinking vessel.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:44.870
It appears that the oil rig is being sucked
down at a dramatic rate.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:58.950
But what causes the shower of debris that
followed remains a matter for intense speculation.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:03.720
Shortly after in May 2008, New York City is
attacked on the evening of Rob's going-away

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.720
party.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.909
His brother, Jason, is killed by what appears
to be a tentacle monster destroying Brooklyn

00:04:08.909 --> 00:04:09.909
bridge.

00:04:09.909 --> 00:04:13.540
Rob finds out that Beth, the girl he's in
love with, is trapped in her apartment.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.411
He sets out to rescue her and is joined by
his late brother's girlfriend, Lily, his friend

00:04:18.411 --> 00:04:22.120
Hud, who serves as the cameraman and Marlena,
a girl from the party.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.460
Marlena gets bit by a parasite and dies.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.960
They save Beth, and Lily gets away on chopper
#402.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:31.841
Rob, Beth and Hud aren't so lucky and that's
where first movie ends.

00:04:31.841 --> 00:04:32.841
But actually there's one more thing though.

00:04:32.841 --> 00:04:33.841
The Cloverfield incident is recorded on Rob's
tape camera.

00:04:33.841 --> 00:04:34.841
It's accidentally recording over Rob and Beth's
trip to Coney Island from one month prior,

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:35.841
where something can be seen falling into the
ocean.

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:36.841
OK, that's where the first movie ends.

00:04:36.841 --> 00:04:42.370
I can't say for sure quite yet, but there's
a good chance that everything in 10 Cloverfield

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:47.949
Lane and it's ARG take place in another dimension,
where the New York City attack hasn't happened

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:48.949
yet.

00:04:48.949 --> 00:04:52.920
And I promise, this all ties back into The
Cloverfield Paradox, so hang with me.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:57.520
In 2009 a military analyst named Howard Stambler
joins Bold Futura, the satellite company I

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.190
told you about, and seven years later he is
honored on Tagruato's website as employee

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.290
of the month.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:07.990
According to the website, Howard’s drive,
commitment and refusal to accept easy answers

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:12.900
resulted in a significant breakthrough diagnosing
transmission complications with two of their

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:13.930
government satellites.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:18.990
At some point, Howard's ex-wife takes custody
of their daughter Megan, and he goes a bit

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:23.370
crazy, creating a website designed to appeal
to her and send her secret messages.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.600
Meanwhile, he's building a doomsday bunker.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:30.210
He later kidnaps young girls and makes them
wear Megan's old clothes to fill the gap left

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.210
my his daughter.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:36.210
In 2016, he uses the secret website to urge
his daughter to runaway from her mother and

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:40.840
come home to take cover in his doomsday shelter,
suggesting that something huge is about to

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.840
happen.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.770
His daughter never shows up, and Howard gets
desperate and finds someone to fill the role

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:49.570
of his daughter during the attack, and that
person is Michelle, the protagonist of 10

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.810
Cloverfield Lane.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:54.930
Howard finds her at the Kelvin gas station,
follows her, knocks her off the road and she

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:55.940
wakes up in the bunker.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:06:00.610
It's just her, Howard, and a man named Emmett
who helped Howard build the bunker.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:04.289
When Emmett and Michelle find out that Howard
was lying about his daughter, they devise

00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:06.320
plans for Michelle to escape.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:09.970
Howard finds out about the plans and kills
Emmett, but Michelle gets out to find that

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.680
the air is clean, but worm-like aliens have
taken over the Earth.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.370
She escapes toward a possible survivors camp
in Austin, which is the end of 10 Cloverfield

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:20.699
Lane, but the ARG extends a little bit past
that.

00:06:20.699 --> 00:06:25.680
A box left by Howard is found containing data
about a particle detector from the International

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:30.790
Space Station that picked up two huge bursts,
followed by a massive red flash that occured

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:35.710
everywhere, presumably the same event described
by Emmett as the beginning of the cataclysm.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:40.750
The next event happens in January 2018, not
long before the release of The Cloverfield

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:45.360
Paradox, so I'm going to go ahead and fire
up that Things You Missed counter.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:46.360
Machine.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.190
That I have.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:52.599
Let's just take a short commercial break while
I do that.

00:06:52.599 --> 00:06:53.599
--

00:06:53.599 --> 00:06:58.490
The ARG for The Cloverfield Paradox actually
began in-real-life in summer 2017 at San Diego

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:02.599
Comic Con, where fans could actually purchase
a Slusho! from the mobile Slusho!

00:07:02.599 --> 00:07:03.949
truck at the event.

00:07:03.949 --> 00:07:07.730
Each Slusho flavor had its own robot mascot,
which is probably due to the fact that the

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:09.770
studio behind the films is Bad Robot.

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:13.550
There is actually a seventh robot, who was
a combination of each flavor.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.960
This seventh robot appeared on the Slusho!

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:16.960
snapchat filter.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:20.520
If you aligned the seventh robot in the blank
space left on the truck and showed the Snapchat

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.520
to the Slusho!

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:25.630
employee, you were asked to fill out a form
to win a prize for solving the puzzle.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.490
That would be just the beginning though.

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:32.550
On January 18th, which happens to be the 10
year anniversary of the original Cloverfield,

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:36.860
the Tagruato website is updated, but upon
trying to access it, you'll receive an error

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:42.080
message, however, examining the image behind
the error message leads to a text post that

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.910
reads as follows:

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:49.920
TOKYO – January 18, 2018
Tagruato has begun development on a revolutionary

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.639
new energy technology.

00:07:51.639 --> 00:07:57.729
In what Ceo Ganu Yoshida called a technological
great leap forward for our planet/ This renewable

00:07:57.729 --> 00:08:01.950
technology will take at least 4 year to complete
with along with another six years international

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:07.890
regulatory bodies to bring the powerful revolutionary
energy source by April 18 2028.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:12.390
I think we can make the conclusion that the
energy technology referenced is "Shepard"

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.530
from The Cloverfield Paradox.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:18.819
I believe that the ARG, like the other two
ARGs before it, takes place in real time,

00:08:18.819 --> 00:08:19.930
here in 2018.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:24.639
The movie, which doesn't occur until the Shepard
exists, takes place in 2028.

00:08:24.639 --> 00:08:29.830
The thing I'm not sure about yet is whether
it takes place in Dimension A, the Cloverfield

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:36.560
universe, Dimension B, the 10 Cloverfield
Lane Universe or Dimensions C and D, two theoretical

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.570
entirely new universes.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.370
I'll give my arguments for each possibility
as we progress.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:46.190
But I think whatever Dimension the movie takes
place in is not our dimension, the one that

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:48.410
you're watching this video in right now.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:52.910
I'd say the internet browsers in that universe
work slightly different, so if we access the

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:57.980
webpage in Google Chrome, Firefox or other
popular web browsers from our universe, the

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.140
page glitches out.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:03.050
I wouldn't rule out the possibility that someone
in our dimension can build a browser that

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:08.020
will read the page properly, maybe we just
haven't discovered it yet in the ARG.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:12.510
Moving forward, not much happens to the website
until January 27th, when it becomes possible

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:16.370
to spot a graphic about something called The
Cloverfield Energy initiative.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:20.800
This time, there is faded handwriting on top
of the graphic, but manipulating the image

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.070
allows us to see the true message.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:26.410
It says "Someone needs to stop this from happening!!!

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:31.260
This is nothing but a cover for a reckless
experiment that will reset the world's grid.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.019
Stop this to save the world.

00:09:33.019 --> 00:09:34.019
T.I.D.O.

00:09:34.019 --> 00:09:35.019
Wave."

00:09:35.019 --> 00:09:38.070
If you'll remember, TIDO Wave is the same
group that opposed Tagruato's deep sea drilling

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:41.459
project back in the era of the original Cloverfield
ARG.

00:09:41.459 --> 00:09:45.350
Also on January 27th, the first winners of
the Slusho!

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:49.430
truck puzzle challenge I mentioned earlier
received their prizes in the mail.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.320
The prize package included a Slusho!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:56.190
bobblehead, a certificate of congratulations
with trademarks registered by Bold Futura,

00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:00.700
the satellite company Howard Stambler worked
for, and a pamphlet version of the Cloverfield

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.740
Energy Initiative graphic spotted on the background
of the Tagruato website.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:10.769
The most recent update to the Tagruato website
introduces a Hebrew news article from 2007

00:10:10.769 --> 00:10:14.350
that talks about road closures near the Dead
Sea, possibly because of sinkholes.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:19.149
As a reminder, that would be a little over
a year before the New York City attack, that

00:10:19.149 --> 00:10:21.899
is, if it even happens on this timeline.

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:27.339
Let's go back to the release date of Tagruato's
new energy source, April 18, 2028.

00:10:27.339 --> 00:10:32.750
If you go to 04182028.com a distorted video
plays.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:36.730
This page also continued to update over the
course of January, and we get little bits

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.930
of information piece by piece from what appears
to be a guy wearing glasses.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:43.290
Some of the lines we can make out include
the following.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:47.810
A male voice says: "That is why I'm trying
to warn you about the dangers of what Tagruato

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:49.240
is trying to do."

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:53.020
In an update, a female voice can be heard
saying, "Welcome to the show...

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.870
Cloverfield Station... joining us today...

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:56.959
controversy...

00:10:56.959 --> 00:10:59.710
Mark Stambler, author of the book..."

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:03.810
So this Mark Stambler has the same last name
as Howard Stambler, the guy who built the

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.860
bunker in 10 Cloverfield Lane.

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:32.540
The latest update from the 04182028 website
looks like this.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:37.370
In case you couldn't make it out, Mark Stambler
says, "This experiment could unleash chaos,

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.370
the likes of which we have never seen.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:42.450
You have no idea how much I would love to
be wrong about this.

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:44.839
It would be no fun for me to be right.

00:11:44.839 --> 00:11:47.430
If you wanna know more, read my book, ..."

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.350
There was also a Mark Stambler Twitter account
at one point.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:54.040
Some users who attempted to DM the account
received a message containing more cryptic

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.040
videos.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:59.100
Unfortunately, they are very hard to decipher
because he actually sent them as vertical

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:03.430
videos of the computer screen as opposed to
just sending the actual video file.

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:07.399
The account is no longer up, and the only
tweets were about some hoax at the university

00:12:07.399 --> 00:12:11.860
he works at and how he had to notify NYPD
about someone watching him.

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:15.580
This information actually doesn't directly
tie into the movie, but I just thought I would

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:19.330
mention it because it tells us more about
the character and it makes me think that someone

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:23.680
from Tagruato has a reason to keep an eye
on this Mark Stambler character.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:28.110
OK, so as of right now, that's as much as
we know from the ARG, but before I tell you

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:31.670
the things you missed from the movie, there
is one more thing that I'd like to point out

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:32.670
in the trailer.

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:35.950
It says 10 years ago, some thing arrived.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:36.950
Now.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:37.950
Find out why.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.950
Then it immediately cuts to a shot of the
Shepard.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:44.610
I would say that could support the idea that
The Cloverfield Paradox takes place in Dimension

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:49.490
A, but the event caused by the firing of the
Shepard could take place across multiple dimensions,

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.639
which I will explain later in this video.

00:12:51.639 --> 00:12:55.790
Early in the movie, Ava and Michael are in
a huge line at a gas station -- and it's the

00:12:55.790 --> 00:13:00.709
fictional Kelvin gas station, which is also
where Michelle stops to get gas in 10 Cloverfield

00:13:00.709 --> 00:13:01.709
Lane.

00:13:01.709 --> 00:13:05.590
If you pause on that shot, you can also get
an idea of how bad the energy crisis discussed

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.089
in the movie really is.

00:13:07.089 --> 00:13:13.000
The sign says "Gas Available Today" as if
that is a rarity and it costs $30 gallon.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:16.959
There’s another appearance towards the end
of the movie which may suggest that Kelvin

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:19.770
was in on the Cloverfield Energy Initiative.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:24.889
When Ava gets back in the car, she asks her
husband if he's moved yet, and he jokes, "forward

00:13:24.889 --> 00:13:25.889
or sideways"?

00:13:25.889 --> 00:13:30.670
However this could also be a foreshadowing
of the journey taken by those aboard the Cloverfield

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:32.180
Station later in this film.

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:36.649
If you're looking at a timeline, they continue
to move forward in time but they also go sideways

00:13:36.649 --> 00:13:38.410
into a different dimension.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:41.710
While we're on this topic, I think now is
a good time to bring up the logo and poster

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.940
of this movie.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:46.460
And before you start to say that it's just
a poster and it doesn't matter, remember that

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:49.459
we have seen clues on the Cloverfield posters
before.

00:13:49.459 --> 00:13:51.779
But this time I specifically want to look
at the logo.

00:13:51.779 --> 00:13:56.500
If we look back to the 10 Cloverfield Lane
Poster it has one timeline leading from the

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.310
Cloverfield text to the place where the movie
takes place.

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:03.370
But this Cloverfield Paradox poster looks
all too familiar for someone who has spent

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:05.360
time studying split timelines.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.710
This logo is definitely supposed to represent
the timelines of the two dimensions occupied

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:11.529
by Cloverfield Station.

00:14:11.529 --> 00:14:14.930
One of them comes off the letter L, which
could mean that the dimension that they travel

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:18.529
to is Dimension B from 10 Cloverfield Lane.

00:14:18.529 --> 00:14:21.769
Before they get their gasoline, there is a
blackout, which Ava says is the fourth or

00:14:21.769 --> 00:14:23.120
fifth one of the day.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:26.680
In both prequels, the calamity started with
a blackout or multiple blackouts.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:27.680
"Ahh!

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:28.680
Oh!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:29.680
Oh God!

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:30.680
Oh my God!

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:31.680
What the hell was that?"

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:38.910
"Power still hasn't been restored to many
cities on the Southern seaboard with this

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.300
afternoon's widespread blackouts."

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:44.801
During the opening title sequence onboard
the station, we see the team picture of the

00:14:44.801 --> 00:14:46.140
international crew.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:49.959
After they cross over to the other dimension
a different photo is seen.

00:14:49.959 --> 00:14:53.860
They also have this tank of worms which are
supposed to be there to consume bacteria,

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:56.079
but they disappear after crossing over.

00:14:56.079 --> 00:15:00.170
Worms are later found inside of Volkov, but
these worms look much smaller than the ones

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.170
in the tank.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:05.170
If the dimension that they travel to really
is Dimension B, then could it be possible

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:09.100
that the disappearance of the worms aboard
the spacecraft is related to the appearance

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:12.779
of vicious worm-like aliens in 10 Cloverfield
Lane?

00:15:12.779 --> 00:15:14.579
Let me know what you think in the comments.

00:15:14.579 --> 00:15:18.149
Ava has a video chat with her husband where
he tries to bring up the idea that maybe they

00:15:18.149 --> 00:15:22.700
should try to have kids again after the accidental
death of their first two kids in a fire.

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:23.700
"We can't go back in time and know what we
know now."

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:27.050
However, the ripple created by the firing
of the Shepard seems to occur at different

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:31.769
places on the timeline in different dimensions,
so maybe the idea of going back in time isn't

00:15:31.769 --> 00:15:33.019
that far fetched.

00:15:33.019 --> 00:15:37.140
It also sets up the later plot point where
Ava finds herself with an opportunity to save

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:39.400
her children in the other dimension.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:42.511
While they are preparing to attempt to fire
up the Shepard again, Acosta tunes into to

00:15:42.511 --> 00:15:47.110
an Earthican TV broadcast and we finally get
to see the full video that had been teased

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:52.149
on the 04182028 website with Mark Stambler
being interviewed live.

00:15:52.149 --> 00:15:58.139
The title of his book is The Cloverfield Paradox
and his Twitter handle is @Paradox_Is_Real,

00:15:58.139 --> 00:16:02.769
which is a real account created in January,
the same time the online portion of the ARG

00:16:02.769 --> 00:16:05.000
started, but it hasn't posted anything yet.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:06.240
Here's what Mark has to say about it.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.240
"That accelerator is 1000x more powerful than
any ever built.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:09.130
Every time they test it they risk ripping
open the membrane of space-time.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:12.269
Smashing together multiple dimensions.

00:16:12.269 --> 00:16:13.830
Shattering reality.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:18.540
And not just on that station.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:19.540
Everywhere.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:23.250
This experiment could unleash chaos.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:29.520
The likes of which we have never seen.

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.520
Monsters.

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:31.520
Demons.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:34.230
Beasts from the sea."

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:40.100
So while this guy may appear to be crazy for
the time being, he turns out to be 100% right,

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.089
so where does he get this information?

00:16:42.089 --> 00:16:46.360
Let's also not forget that Mark's brother,
Howard Stambler knew exactly when the calamity

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:50.440
was going to hit in 10 Cloverfield Lane and
what it was going to entail.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:54.829
In the ARG he tried to get his daughter to
come down to his bunker well in advance.

00:16:54.829 --> 00:16:58.839
He jknows he's low on time before the disaster
happens, so he knocks Michelle off of the

00:16:58.839 --> 00:16:59.839
road.

00:16:59.839 --> 00:17:03.699
Emmett explains that he was nearby right then
the huge flash hit and he raced straight to

00:17:03.699 --> 00:17:06.770
the bunker, where Howard was already closing
the door.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:10.329
Howard knew exactly how to prepare for what
was coming and he did.

00:17:10.329 --> 00:17:14.449
So the question is: how did these brothers
effectively predict the future when nobody

00:17:14.449 --> 00:17:15.449
else could?

00:17:15.449 --> 00:17:17.949
That could be a question answered in another
movie.

00:17:17.949 --> 00:17:19.160
Let's continue Mark's speech.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:21.589
"But not just here and now.

00:17:21.589 --> 00:17:22.800
In the past.

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:24.010
In the future.

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:25.230
In other dimensions."

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:29.380
This could be the key to understanding how
everything we've seen so far is linked.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:33.250
Let's assume for a moment that we're dealing
with four entirely different dimensions.

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:37.870
Maybe at the time that the Shepard overloads
in Dimension C, Dimension A is still only

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:41.490
in 2008, so the Cloverfield incident occurs.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:46.880
Maybe at that same time in Dimension B, it's
still 2016, so the 10 Cloverfield Lane attack

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:47.880
hits.

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:52.230
And maybe Dimension D is parallel, and the
event destroys their Cloverfield station.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:56.650
There is more evidence outside of just taking
Mark Stambler's word for it to suggest that

00:17:56.650 --> 00:18:00.670
this is one event taking place in multiple
timelines at different times.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:04.770
Let's revisit Emmett's description of the
event that triggered the cataclysm in 10 Cloverfield

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:05.770
Lane.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.130
"The attack I saw myself."

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:08.820
"What do you mean?"

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.840
"I was on my way home from work.

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:16.610
And it looked like a flash.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.200
Bright red.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.450
Like an explosion from way far off.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:22.799
Wasn't like fireworks.

00:18:22.799 --> 00:18:27.260
No this was more like something you read about
in the bible."

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:33.520
"So what you saw, what a flash of light?

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:34.520
Lightning?

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:38.700
A fire that flared up?"

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.549
"I'm not explaining it right.

00:18:41.549 --> 00:18:43.760
This wasn't like anything I'd ever seen."

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:47.450
Seems awfully familiar after seeing The Cloverfield
Paradox.

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:50.810
Another connection to 10 Cloverfield Lane
can be found in Michael’s social media feed

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.540
after the first explosion.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:55.799
First of all, I do hope we’re running on
a 7G network in 10 years.

00:18:55.799 --> 00:19:00.190
But the posts are all talking about a huge
noise, several missing city blocks and part

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:01.320
of the city in rubble.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.220
But one of the posts is a question asking
if anyone’s been outside and wondering if

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.720
the air is safe to breathe.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:10.690
A quick note, when Michael saves the little
girl, he puts on a Cartoon for her called

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:15.210
Bleep Bloop, which appears to be about the
mascot of the production company Bad Robot,

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:18.750
but could also have something to do with the
robot flavors seen on the side of the Slusho!

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:19.750
truck.

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:22.880
It’s more likely a reference to Bad Robot,
since in the credits it says the animation

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:27.809
was created by JJ Abrams and Ben Schwartz
and Bad Robot is JJ Abrams’s company.

00:19:27.809 --> 00:19:29.400
Here's another interesting bit.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:33.760
During the Shepard overload, the whole station
starts shaking and we see a shot of the Slusho!

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:38.510
bobblehead, the same one that Comic-Con fans
in 2017 were given for solving the Slusho!

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:39.510
puzzle!

00:19:39.510 --> 00:19:42.980
This is the first of many parallels to the
first Cloverfield movie.

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:46.760
Another theory that I have is that the dimension
that The Cloverfield Paradox takes place in

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:50.620
is the same as Dimension A except for the
fact that the Cloverfield incident hasn't

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:51.670
happened yet.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:55.120
This time instead of happening in New York
City, it's happening in Space.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.590
An early reference to Slusho!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.880
just before the disaster strikes is just one
of many parallels we'll see.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:03.840
When they find as rescue Mina, she has a beam
lodged into her shoulder in the same spot

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:08.190
that Beth is impaled by a beam when they rescue
her in the original Cloverfield.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:11.970
Speaking of Beth, she reaches out to Rob via
her cell phone to let him know she’s trapped

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:12.970
in her apartment.

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.150
In The Cloverfield Paradox, Michael reads
on his cell phone about one of his friends

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:17.830
being trapped in an apartment after the calamity
hits.

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:23.830
The person is trapped in 402 Pa St. That may
or may not be related to helicopter #402 which

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:26.669
Lily gets away in during the first movie.

00:20:26.669 --> 00:20:30.600
In this shot we can see a monster in the background
wrecking a city with huge skyscrapers.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:34.810
It’s assumed this is somewhere in the UK
but we never find out what city it is.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:39.159
And finally, in order to save the space station,
they have to prevent it from tilting off axis

00:20:39.159 --> 00:20:40.390
by 25°.

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:44.850
Beth’s apartment is also tilting off axis
by just under 25°.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:49.270
They end up going to the building next to
it and the three main characters have to traverse

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:52.350
the ruins of the roof to get to the door that
they need to get to.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:55.581
The scene where the astronauts had to cross
over to get to the other part of the space

00:20:55.581 --> 00:20:56.890
station is almost identical.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:59.230
And then there’s the villain of the movie.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:03.140
In this movie, Mina is portrayed as the villain,
even though she’s just trying to help her

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:04.140
own planet.

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:07.520
We don’t know a whole lot about Clover but
it appears that the destruction caused by

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:10.460
it is just due to self defense instincts as
well.

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:14.210
When we first discover Mina they hear the
sounds of Clover’s roar on the other side

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.210
of the wall.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.280
And when Mina is on the attack at the end
of the movie we can also hear the distant

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:30.850
sound of that roar.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:35.320
And of course, Cloverfield ends with a mysterious
object, which is assumed to be a satellite

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:39.630
or space shuttle, crashing into the Atlantic
Ocean, which is exactly where the pod from

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.920
The Cloverfield Paradox lands.

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:45.860
And while this does answer some questions
about what caused the calamity in each movie,

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:47.850
it also raises plenty of questions.

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:52.039
What role did Tagruato have in the opening
of this space-time tear?

00:21:52.039 --> 00:21:53.770
And how do all of these films fit together?

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:57.350
I’m going to talk about the three most plausible
scenarios.

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:58.660
Scenario Number One.

00:21:58.660 --> 00:22:03.060
The Cloverfield Paradox takes place in it’s
own universe -- Dimension C. The firing of

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:07.350
the Shepard causes time-space tears in all
four Dimensions and monsters, creatures from

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:10.850
the sea and demons travel to earth through
these tears.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:15.200
The event pushes Cloverfield Station into
Dimension D and when they overload the Shepard

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:18.280
again, they push themselves back into Dimension
C.

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:22.740
This would explain why there is never any
mention of a previous calamity in either sequel

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:26.610
and why Clover appears to be much much bigger
than the monster in Cloverfield.

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:32.100
This is the easiest and least creative scenario,
and wastes the opportunity to tie in the object

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:36.419
landing at the end of Cloverfield to the shuttle
landing in Paradox.

00:22:36.419 --> 00:22:37.690
Scenario Number Two.

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:42.340
The Cloverfield Paradox takes place in Dimension
A, 20 years after the New York Cloverfield

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:43.440
incident.

00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:47.409
After the events of Cloverfield, the monster
is captured or goes back into hiding.

00:22:47.409 --> 00:22:52.309
However, an accident caused by Yoshida Medical
Research causes their Cellular Growth Accelerant

00:22:52.309 --> 00:22:57.789
used for healing injured humans to blow Clover
up to a much bigger more destructive size.

00:22:57.789 --> 00:23:02.000
When they fire the Shepard this process is
sped up and it creates a disaster on Earth,

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:04.870
while the space station is pushed into Dimension
B.

00:23:04.870 --> 00:23:09.059
The Paradox causes a huge flash which gets
the attention of the aliens -- possibly the

00:23:09.059 --> 00:23:10.059
Martians

00:23:10.059 --> 00:23:13.601
"Russians are developing some nasty stuff
and if the Martians finally figured out a

00:23:13.601 --> 00:23:20.130
way to get here, their weapons will make the
Ruskies like sticks and stones."

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:22.460
Who set to wipe out human life on the Earth.

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:28.230
They fire the Shepard again and come back
to Dimension A at the end to find it in ruins.

00:23:28.230 --> 00:23:29.610
Scenario Number Three.

00:23:29.610 --> 00:23:34.980
The Cloverfield Paradox takes place in Dimension
C. The Shepard tears space-time so that disasters

00:23:34.980 --> 00:23:40.750
also happen in 2008 and 2016 in Dimension
A and B respectively.

00:23:40.750 --> 00:23:46.000
When the Shepard is fired they travel to Dimension
B or D, but when it is fired again to get

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:51.270
back home, they actually unknowingly go to
Dimension A, which is similar to their Dimension,

00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:54.460
but Clover has been growing and on the loose
for over 20 years.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:58.290
But that of course still doesn’t solve the
question of what landed in the water at the

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:00.100
end of Cloverfield.

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:01.350
Unless…

00:24:01.350 --> 00:24:06.400
Scenario Number Four -- they went back in
time to 2008 Dimension A, but that doesn’t

00:24:06.400 --> 00:24:11.230
explain why Clover is awake and GIANT at the
time of their landing, while in Cloverfield

00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:14.200
there was no issue until a month after the
object landed.

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:18.320
There are so many possibilities here so if
you have your own theories leave in the comments,

00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:22.020
I’d love to piece this one together, but
chances are we won’t get answers until a

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:23.200
future movie.

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:27.400
And there’s also a possibility that the
ARG for this movie isn’t over yet, so if

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:30.909
you’d like to see me cover any updates we
might see, let hear you in the comments on

00:24:30.909 --> 00:24:31.909
that as well.

00:24:31.909 --> 00:24:35.790
If you were confused at any point in this
video, go ahead and leave a like.

00:24:35.790 --> 00:24:40.620
My name is CZ and I love talking about psychological
horror, but honestly my brain is pretty racked

00:24:40.620 --> 00:24:41.870
on this one.

00:24:41.870 --> 00:24:46.250
But regardless I’ll be back with new horrors
every week so make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld

00:24:46.250 --> 00:24:51.240
and ring the deathbell so you can see those,
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:53.019
Assuming we both survive.

